{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on your CDF-1 results 85fed53d.\n\n1. Scope-typed fields: accepted, no change. Write the six writer\n   classes, the count of 45 sites and the `task.lane` fact into\n   the report. Add one duty there: a definition for\n   `platform:task` checks the kind of the lane where it reads the\n   lane.\n\n2. Timed turns: accepted, no change.\n\n3. Retained births: build the cap. Retained births and retained\n   copies count against `scopeBytes` in every scope. The stop is\n   a host storage stop: the input writes no entry and gets\n   `scope-full` with `scopeBytes`, as the opt-in answers today.\n   No cap for one entry in this head.\n\nKernel. `packages/scope` is a platform service in section 3 of\n`docs/kernel.md`. The cap adds no export, no reason code and no\nrecord form, so section 7 asks for no kernel review. The checker\nreviews the head with the Security conclusion.\n\nThe head. CDF-1 (27cb5f60) takes one head, after RC-1 in the gate\norder. It carries:\n- the cap, with the witness that fails at 57e893c0,\n- the three results in \"Faults found after the composed head\",\n- the comment at `directory.ts:431`,\n- item 4 of IDR-1: the comments of `packages/contract/src` that\n  say \"incarnation\" for a genesis.\n\nBefore the code, send me one act: whether the count is a stored\ntotal or a scan, what a scope made before the head does at its\nfirst turn, and what a scope that is already past the cap\nanswers. If the count adds stored state, the head lands before\nthe cutover deployment.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}